        "reasoning": "I'm planning a static armoured convoy hauler model with a cab, armoured plates, wheels, and a sealed cargo pod, roughly 9m long, 3m wide, and 3.4m tall, facing +Z.\n\nLaying out the chassis, three wheel axles with fenders and glowing hub caps, and a two-tier cab with a sloped windshield and cyan glow visor...\n\nNow adding the front details -- bull bar with hazard stripes, glowing headlights, exhaust stacks behind the cab, and a sealed hexagonal cargo capsule mounted on a ribbed cradle frame.\n\nI'm giving the pod end caps and an amber seal band, flat emblem surfaces, angled armor side plates, a small roof turret with barrels, thin antenna masts, and neon underglow strips, while checking the pod sits properly cradled over the chassis.\n\nNow I'm checking the pod's overlap with the cab—since the front cap at z=1.3 would intrude into the cab by over two units, I'll use flat-capped octagonal sweep caps instead of rounded ones to avoid the collision.\n\nFor the rear end, I'll add a tapered frustum section from radius 0.6 to 1.05, extending slightly past the chassis edge, which should look fine. Then I'm setting up color constants, a box helper, and verifying wheel placement so the 0.62-radius wheels sit flush with the ground at y=0.62.\n\nWriting cylinder helper and detail code...\n\nI'm pulling in a glow effect from the kit for the lights, detailing wheels with dark tires, steel rims, and a cyan-glowing hub, using low-poly octagonal tire sides instead of individual tread boxes, then mirroring components across the x-axis to finish the layout.\n\n"
